  <data name="Prompt.WhoAmI" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>drangoht — github.com/drangoht

This site lists the account's public repositories. It is written in .NET,
server-rendered, bilingual, and deployed in a container. Its own repository
is in the list.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Prompt.Cache" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The catalogue comes from the GitHub API, then from a cache while it holds.
An on-disk copy takes over when the API stops answering: the site keeps
serving the last known list rather than an empty page.

No token is required. Without one, GitHub grants sixty requests per hour —
far more than the cache consumes.</value>
  </data>
